$CATEGORY: Q19 - ArrayList (deck)

::Q1901::
pseudocode - A way of designing programs by writing rough drafts in a combination of English and Java. {TRUE}

::Q1902::
A method that implements part of a more complex algorithm; often it is not particularly useful on its own. {
    = helper method
    ~ wrapper method
}

::Q1903::
bottom-up design - Breaking down a problem into subproblems, and solving each subproblem one at a time. {FALSE}

::Q1904::
A simple sorting algorithm that searches for the smallest or largest element n times.{
    = selection method
    ~ merge method
}

::Q1905::
A recursive sorting algorithm that divides an array into two parts, sorts each part  and merges the results.{
    = merge method
    ~ selection method
}

::Q1906::
off-by-one - a common programming mistake that results in iterating two time too many, or too few. {FALSE}

::Q1907::
static context - The parts of a class that run without reference to a specific instance of the class. {TRUE}

::Q1908::
collection - a Java library class, like ArrayList, that represents a group of objects. {TRUE}

::Q1909::
A method that calls another method without doing much additional work. {
    ~ helper method
    = wrapper method
}
